      "changeSets": {
        "1": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 176,
                "quote": "| Some _ -> Error(BackupExists path)"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 195,
                "quote": "let owed = library.Members |> Map.toList |> List.sumBy (fun (id, _) -> Accounts.owed id library)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The new rule that a backup may not overwrite an existing one is decided in the Tier 3 use case `backup`. It is not decided in Tier 2. The code only adds the `BackupExists` error value to Tier 1. This is the 'whether something is allowed' kind of decision that the criterion puts in Tier 1/2. `backupInfo` also derives the library-wide owed total in Tier 3, by summing `Accounts.owed` across members. Per-member owed comes from Tier 2, but the total is a Tier 3 derivation. `restore` and the summary are plain projections and carry no rule.",
            "score": 0
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Host/Cli/CommandLine.fs",
                "line": 195,
                "quote": "| Ok [ \"backup\"; path ] -> UseCases.backup ports path |> render showBackup"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 175,
                "quote": "match ports.Archive.Load path with"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "All new file effects go through the existing `Archive` and `Store` ports. The old CLI code called `JsonFileStore.create path` directly from presentation. The change set removes it, and the CLI now only calls Tier 3 use cases. No effect is added in Tier 1/2, and no Tier 4 code calls Tier 2.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "`Views.summary` is the single definition of the library summary. It is used by `backup`, `restore` and `backupInfo`, and `summaryText` in the CLI is a single formatter shared by all three views. The owed amount reuses `Accounts.owed` and `Views.money`. The error texts are defined once in `describeError`. No fact is restated.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Catalog.fs",
                "line": 18,
                "quote": "do! ensure (not (library.Members.ContainsKey memberId)) (DuplicateMember memberId)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The new rules are the refusal when the backup lacks the member, the refusal when the member already exists, and the choice of which data is taken: the member's fines and payments only. They are all in the Tier 2 function `Catalog.restoreMember`, which reuses `DuplicateMember`. The Tier 3 `restoreMember` use case only loads the archive, calls Tier 2 through `commit`, and builds a view. Tier 1 gains the `BackupLacksMember` error.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "`Catalog.restoreMember` is pure. The backup is read through the existing `Archive` port, and the result is persisted through the existing `commit` helper and `Store` port. The CLI only dispatches to the use case and renders the view. No new effect appears in Tier 1/2 or in presentation.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Catalog.fs",
                "line": 23,
                "quote": "Fines = library.Fines @ (backup.Fines |> List.filter (fun fine -> fine.Member = memberId))"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Catalog.fs",
                "line": 24,
                "quote": "Payments = library.Payments @ (backup.Payments |> List.filter (fun payment -> payment.Member = memberId))"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 204,
                "quote": "Fines = (Accounts.finesOf m.Id library).Length"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The predicate 'a fine or payment belongs to a member' is written inline in `Catalog.restoreMember`. `Accounts.finesOf` and `Accounts.paymentsOf` already express it, and the new view code uses them. The two copies agree today, but they could drift. The error values and the duplicate-member rule are reused, not redefined.",
            "score": 1
          }
